{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXDWtwpFmpYqW6mLy9DT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VHmRzBg3qPjPq9x8K1tUk8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/hc/72kc25qn4z360jql9zgjgl5w0000gn/T/neuron-demo-planner-oluzp6ha/w/specs/feature-1-comment-editing.md","content":"# Feature 1: Comment editing\n\nPUT /api/articles/:slug/comments/:id with body {\"comment\":{\"body\":\"...\"}}. The comment author may edit their own comment within the edit window. A successful edit sets the edited marker.\n\n## Rules used (source note in brackets; values not copied here)\n- Edit permission and time window: policy-edit-window.md\n- Owner field authorId: code-comment-ownership.md\n- Comment fields: code-comment-model.md\n- Edited marker and its migration rule: policy-edited-at-marker.md\n- Migration folder layout and apply command: code-migrations.md\n- Release checks and per-migration undo note: policy-release-checklist.md\n- Error body shape: policy-error-response.md. Conflict: code-error-shape.md shows a different 401 body. For new errors I followed policy-error-response.md.\n- Status codes: code-error-shape.md (validation, missing token, other errors). Gap: no rule sets the status for an edit refused by the window or by a non-author. Not decided here.\n- Token header: code-auth-header.md\n- Unit tests: code-test-layout.md\n\n## Steps\n1. Migration adding editedAt. It must not change existing rows. Include the undo note.\n2. Service: load comment by id, check author and window, update body and editedAt.\n3. Route: PUT handler. Errors use the rule shape.\n4. Unit tests in the services folder, with the mocked database.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4656,"cache_read_input_tokens":3468,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4656,"ephemeral_1h_inp