{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXDYUr2f2JD7u6vcGtUD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the spec to `specs/feature-1-comment-editing.md`. It lists each rule by name and source note, with no values copied in. One rule is missing, and one pair of notes disagrees.\n\n**Answers to the six questions (from the notes; values are kept out of the spec):**\n\n1. **Who may edit:** only the comment's author. Source: `policy-edit-window.md`. The author is identified by `authorId` (`code-comment-ownership.md`).\n2. **Edit window:** the edit is allowed for a fixed number of minutes after `createdAt`. After that the API refuses it. Source: `policy-edit-window.md`.\n3. **Edited mark:** a nullable `editedAt` timestamp, null until the first edit, set to the edit time on each successful edit. The migration that adds it must not change existing rows. Source: `policy-edited-at-marker.md`. The model has no `editedAt` yet (`code-comment-model.md`).\n4. **Error shape and status codes:** new errors use `{\"errors\": {field: [messages]}}` with no extra wrapper (`policy-error-response.md`). The status codes come from `code-error-shape.md`: validation errors, missing or bad token, and other errors each have a status.\n5. **Migrations:** one timestamped folder per migration under `app/src/prisma/migrations`. Applied with `npx prisma migrate deploy`, using `DATABASE_URL` (`code-migrations.md`). Before shipping, run that command against a fresh database, and give each new migration a one-line undo note (`policy-release-checklist.md`).\n6. **Unit tests:** Jest files named `*.test.ts` under `app/src/tests/services` and `app/src/tests/utils`. Run with `npx nx test api`. The database is mocked, so no Postgres is needed (`code-test-layout.md`).\n\n**Gaps and conflicts:**\n\n- **Missing rule:** no note gives the HTTP status for an edit refused because the window has passed, or for an edit by someone other than the author. I did not invent one. The spec marks this as a gap. The delete path returns 404 with an empty body, but that is current code for deletion, not a rule for editing, so I did not reuse it.\n- **Conflict:** `code-error-shape.md` describes the 401 body as `{\"status\":\"error\",\"message\":...}`. `policy-error-response.md` says new errors use the `errors` shape. The 401 is an existing response, not a new one, so the conflict does not change this feature's new error responses. For new errors I followed `policy-error-response.md`.\n\nI did not read `app/` or change any code. The spec has four steps: the migration, the service check, the route, and the unit tests."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5004,"cache_read_input_tokens":8124,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5004,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9b82773f-8b36-4263-880c-b0a6da327e22","uuid":"b3e8680f-e828-41fc-87db-7f48e97019e9","timestamp":"2026-10-29T21:12:15.284Z","request_id":"req_011CgXDYUSiSxSbQwzAgMZFh"}
